{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788036565539508527,"compiled_state":{"alias":"candied-senseless-squirrel","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":4,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"b34f08e59a0e4870f995c810bbf310e428d427d249eceb18430a2623580445ff","event_uuid":"f699f890-77ae-4f9c-8502-686a01d305c9","position":{"commit_sha":"bd638f2b1414e92369ebd1f25c55fff46a3cdf77","position":"1788033535584801407-f699f890-77ae-4f9c-8502-686a01d305c9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"433aad73047d250a06cfd46ee34fc62ae9ec950d31ee08d65e961362deadb947","event_uuid":"062b1ac0-747a-4aa7-a2c8-232b9f184ef3","position":{"commit_sha":"fc078d5c0c60acf7e55fed289ef27d637706f5d6","position":"1788033568721269496-062b1ac0-747a-4aa7-a2c8-232b9f184ef3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"c48b8f468eae215a3f9b698132eec5601a175b74467f511e533fa999817319eb","event_uuid":"8ef3bd6a-40b2-4a59-82d4-a6d76f84fe8d","position":{"commit_sha":"40c89fc12adfa1eac7881cd22eba28d123fc2f0f","position":"1788033588021601680-8ef3bd6a-40b2-4a59-82d4-a6d76f84fe8d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"a38316db89928c13f17db32f32200ba29148a7cc0efea887f996228ba212bd17","event_uuid":"d20e8fa3-091e-496b-9d94-d12405bdf858","position":{"commit_sha":"4c1ed25e134681cdb4e19d876918314904a16e72","position":"1788036565539508526-d20e8fa3-091e-496b-9d94-d12405bdf858"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788033535584801407,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"8ef3bd6a-40b2-4a59-82d4-a6d76f84fe8d","relation":"blocks","target_id":"ec44-b572-1067-4c52"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nMaking OperationSnapshot authoritative for LLM operations (gaudy-working-mantaray) migrates `LLMConfig.from_env` call sites and threads a snapshot-derived projection through the gate/workflow entry points. The two llm modules carrying the densest from_env/composition logic are within a few lines of the hard 800-LOC module-size cap (`.github/module-size-limit.txt` = 800), so that threading would breach the CI module-size gate on first edit:\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/config.py` = 799 (`LLMConfig.from_env` plus 14 from_env/gate references)\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py` = 796\n\nCreate headroom FIRST via behavior-preserving extraction along existing call-graph seams so the config-threading cutover lands without breaching the module-size gate. This story adds no snapshot-threading logic; it only relocates existing clusters.\n\n## Approach\n\nExtract cohesive existing clusters into sibling modules per the AGENTS.md module-size policy (existing seams only; target 200-500 LOC; never create a module < 100 LOC; never split mechanically):\n\n- `llm/config.py`: move the primitive env/file reader helpers (`_env_truthy`, `_read_llm_file_table`, `_llm_str_source`, `_llm_str`, `_llm_int`, `_llm_float`, `_llm_drain_mode`) into a new sibling module `llm/config_readers.py`. `config.py` re-imports every one of them (`from .config_readers import (...)  # noqa: F401`) at module top level, mirroring the EXISTING `gate_context` re-export pattern documented in `config.py`'s own L41-47 docstring. `LLMConfig.from_env` (the sole in-repo caller of this cluster) is NOT moved and keeps calling these names as bare references — so its lookup resolves through `config.py`'s own namespace (its `__globals__`), exactly as `from_env` already does for the re-exported `gate_context` names. This is what keeps the ~15 existing `monkeypatch.setattr(rebar.llm.config, \"_read_llm_file_table\", ...)` (and sibling helper) test seams live: the patch rebinds `config.py`'s module attribute, and `from_env`'s bare-name call reads that same attribute at call time. `src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py` also imports `_read_llm_file_table` directly from `rebar.llm.config` — it keeps working unchanged because the re-export preserves that import path.\n- `llm/plan_review/__init__.py`: move ONLY the five pure/leaf functions of the score-floor / completion-floor cluster — `_apply_floor_to_verdict`, `_score_floor_novelty`, `_apply_completion_floor_to_verdict`, `_classify_completion`, `_group_blocking_fix_units` — into a new sibling module `llm/plan_review/floors.py`, re-imported into `__init__.py` (`from .floors import (...)  # noqa: F401`). The two orchestrator wrappers, `_maybe_apply_rising_floor` and `_maybe_apply_completion_floor`, STAY in `__init__.py` (not moved) because they are both (a) the entry points `_run_plan_review` calls directly, and (b) the functions whose internal calls to the five moved leaves must keep resolving through `__init__.py`'s own namespace so that `monkeypatch.setattr(plan_review, \"_score_floor_novelty\", ...)` (test_plan_review_rising_floor.py) and `monkeypatch.setattr(plan_review, \"_classify_completion\", ...)` (test_completion_floor.py) continue to intercept the call as today. `monkeypatch.setattr(plan_review, \"_maybe_apply_rising_floor\"/\"_maybe_apply_completion_floor\"/\"_group_blocking_fix_units\", ...)` (test_plan_review_sidecar_heldout.py) keeps working regardless, because its caller `_run_plan_review` also stays in `__init__.py`. This mirrors the same config.py/gate_context precedent: never move a caller and callee apart when a test monkeypatches the callee through the caller's original module.\n\n`LLMConfig`, `review_plan`, and the public plan_review imports keep working; only internal call sites for the five moved plan_review leaves change module (moving with them), while `from_env`'s and the two floor-wrapper's own call sites are untouched.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/` — extract the named clusters into new sibling modules (`config_readers.py`, `plan_review/floors.py`) and update imports only. Does NOT modify `src/rebar/llm/runner.py`, which is owned by the runner refactor (hurt-antigorite-genet), to avoid a collision.\n- `tests/unit/`, `tests/unit/workflow/`, and `tests/external/` — import-path updates only (e.g. `from rebar.llm import config as llm_config` keeps resolving unchanged since re-exports preserve every existing attribute path); no assertion changes.\n\n## Testing\n\nExisting llm and plan-review suites (including `tests/unit/workflow/` and `tests/external/`) pass unchanged (behavior-preserving) — in particular every existing `monkeypatch.setattr(rebar.llm.config, \"_read_llm_file_table\", ...)` site and every `monkeypatch.setattr(plan_review, \"<floor-helper>\", ...)` site in `test_plan_review_rising_floor.py`, `test_completion_floor.py`, `test_completion_floor_e2e.py`, `test_blocking_fix_unit_grouping.py`, and `test_plan_review_sidecar_heldout.py` keeps intercepting the same call it does today. Module-size gate, per-function complexity ratchet, lint, and typecheck pass. No new CI-provider, network, or Docker dependency is introduced (portable default suite).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `llm/config.py` and `llm/plan_review/__init__.py` are each comfortably below 800 LOC (target <= 700), achieved only by extracting existing call-graph clusters into sibling modules (`config_readers.py`, `plan_review/floors.py`).\n- [ ] No newly created module is below 100 LOC, and no extraction is mechanical.\n- [ ] Every existing monkeypatch seam targeting a moved helper via its ORIGINAL module (`rebar.llm.config.<helper>` / `rebar.llm.plan_review.<helper>`) keeps intercepting the same call site it does today — proven by running the existing suite unedited, with zero test-file changes required for the seam itself.\n- [ ] Behavior is unchanged: existing llm/provider/plan-review suites (`tests/unit/`, `tests/unit/workflow/`, `tests/external/`) pass with no edits beyond import paths.\n- [ ] `src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py`'s direct `from rebar.llm.config import _read_llm_file_table` (or equivalent) keeps working unchanged.\n- [ ] `llm/runner.py` is not modified here, avoiding collision with hurt-antigorite-genet.\n- [ ] Module-size gate, per-function complexity ratchet, lint, and typecheck all pass.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/config.py","reason":"Extract primitive env/file reader helpers into a sibling so from_env threading has headroom."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py","reason":"Extract the score-floor / completion-floor cluster into a sibling to create headroom."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["blocks","ec44-b572-1067-4c52"],["parent","eb64-844b-ab7a-4915"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"eb64-844b-ab7a-4915","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["llm","refactor","module-size"],"ticket_id":"02b7-82ef-ca69-4aa8","ticket_type":"story","title":"Create llm config-threading module-size headroom before the authoritative-snapshot cutover","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f699f890-77ae-4f9c-8502-686a01d305c9","062b1ac0-747a-4aa7-a2c8-232b9f184ef3","8ef3bd6a-40b2-4a59-82d4-a6d76f84fe8d","d20e8fa3-091e-496b-9d94-d12405bdf858"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788036565539508527,"uuid":"32d5a618-17b3-48b0-8034-b66e7446c4b8"}